{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>הוות</b> — It says about the tongue 'you devise,' because the tongue is like an interpreter, and through it the thought is seen." "And the meaning of הוות — things that come into being according to your thoughts. Some say: it means guile, from 'תרמיש בים' (cast into the sea). And some say: from the root of מרמה (deceit), for the root is one."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 52, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:38.804303895Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}